cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Solutions Table: a CIS-grounded Solutions dimension for the Security Cards"
message: "If you use this deck, the materials, or the application, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Hsiao An
    family-names: Wang
    affiliation: Northeastern University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-6967-3904"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hsjwang/solutions-table"
abstract: >-
  A fifth dimension for the University of Washington Security Cards. Twenty-one
  defensive control cards mapped to the CIS Critical Security Controls v8.1 at
  safeguard level, seven zero-cost modifier cards carrying architectural and
  risk-treatment principles, ten scenarios with expert keys, facilitator
  materials, and a browser implementation that exports the artifacts a study
  scores. Card cost is derived from CIS Implementation Group tier rather than
  designer judgment, and the budget is calibrated so that trade-offs are forced
  rather than nominal.
keywords:
  - cybersecurity education
  - game-based learning
  - serious games
  - CIS Controls
  - cybersecurity clinics
  - risk assessment
